{# Widget "kpis" — the day's figures, the design's five cards.

   THE HOUSE KPI CARD AND NOTHING BESPOKE: `.grid.kstrip` of `.c.kpi`, each a
   `.tab`, a `.disp` figure with its denominator, and one `.sub` fragment. The
   strip idiom and the card idiom are the only two the house has.

   EVERY FIGURE IS A COUNT, NEVER A VERDICT. The plan says who was due; the
   AREA says what its handsets reported; the numbers are the sizes of the sets
   that fall out. Nothing here is stored and nothing is re-derived.

   AN AREA WITH NO POST ON THE BOOKS IS NOT A PARK SCORING NOUGHT. It gets the
   empty state, because 0 of 0 reporting is an accusation nobody made. #}
{% if not dash.figures.day.hasABook %}
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">The day&rsquo;s check-ins</span>
        <div class="rfrag"><b>No post is on the roster&rsquo;s books</b><em>the area registers {{ dash.figures.day.postsInTheArea }} station{{ dash.figures.day.postsInTheArea == 1 ? '' : 's' }}; a watch is given to a post deliberately, so none is assumed</em></div>
    </div>
{% else %}
<div class="grid kstrip">
    <div class="c kpi hot" data-kpi="checked-in">
        <span class="tab">Checked in<span class="src">&middot; <time datetime="{{ dash.day.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ dash.day.format('D j M')|lower }}</time></span></span>
        <b class="disp">{{ dash.figures.day.checkedIn }}<em>of {{ dash.figures.day.expected }}</em></b>
        <span class="sub">{{ dash.figures.day.expected - dash.figures.day.checkedIn }} the area has read nothing for</span>
    </div>
    <div class="c kpi" data-kpi="verified">
        <span class="tab">At post &middot; verified</span>
        <b class="disp">{{ dash.figures.day.verified }}<em>of {{ dash.figures.day.verified + dash.figures.day.flagged }} claiming</em></b>
        <span class="sub">the pings sit inside the catchment</span>
    </div>
    {# FLAGGED AND NO CHECK-IN ARE ONE CARD, and the fold is the ruling's:
       a row is four cards, never five. They belong together anyway — both
       are a person somebody has to go and ask about — and the fragment
       keeps the two apart, because a claim the pings disagree with and a
       claim nobody made are answered differently. #}
    <div class="c kpi{{ dash.figures.needingAnAnswer > 0 ? ' bad' : '' }}" data-kpi="needs-an-answer">
        <span class="tab">Needs an answer</span>
        <b class="disp">{{ dash.figures.needingAnAnswer }}</b>
        <span class="sub">
            {%- if dash.figures.needingAnAnswer > 0 %}<span class="r">{{ dash.figures.day.flagged }} unverified &middot; {{ dash.figures.day.noCheckIn }} no check-in</span>
            {%- else %}every claim is borne out and everybody due has reported{% endif -%}
        </span>
    </div>
    <div class="c kpi" data-kpi="posts-reporting">
        <span class="tab">Posts reporting</span>
        <b class="disp">{{ dash.figures.day.postsReporting }}<em>of {{ dash.figures.day.postsOnTheBooks }}</em></b>
        <span class="sub">of the area&rsquo;s {{ dash.figures.day.postsInTheArea }} registered</span>
    </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
